`selexprep_catalog.csv` is the canonical flat source used to build the
`selexprep_public_catalog` package dataset. It contains 240 public HT-SELEX
deposits from ENA, Figshare, and Zenodo, with eight curated experimental fields
and a reconciliation status for each field.

The snapshot was migrated byte-for-byte from Python selexprep v0.4.6
(commit 63f33b44bb381c2c6b6ed131f3b98e8d6ff9d5f5). Run
`inst/scripts/make-selexprep-public-catalog.R` from the package source root to
verify its SHA-256, schema, identifiers, and statuses before rebuilding the
`.rda` dataset.

The catalog compilation and curation annotations are MIT-licensed, as in
the pinned upstream selexprep source. The original MIT notice is retained in
inst/licenses/selexprep-MIT.txt. Source records, papers and sequencing reads
have separate terms; see inst/DATA_LICENSES.md. See `inst/CATALOG_PROVENANCE.md` for sources, curation disclosure, and
immutable provenance links.

This is a frozen discovery snapshot, not a live availability claim. Before
downloading ENA data, use `inspect_selexprep_accession()` to obtain current
records and verify that an accession is still available.

`ena-inspection.rds` is a dated public metadata snapshot supporting offline
examples. See inst/ENA_EXAMPLE_PROVENANCE.md for sources, checksum and terms.

The cs_round_*.fastq.gz files are real CC BY 4.0 DL-SELEX R1 subsets. See
inst/REAL_DATA_PROVENANCE.md for attribution, checksums and reconstruction.
